	"transcription": [
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:00,000",
				"to": "00:00:03,200"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 0,
				"to": 3200
			},
			"text": " What would happen if one tried to funnel Niagara Falls through a straw?"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:03,200",
				"to": "00:00:05,440"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 3200,
				"to": 5440
			},
			"text": " The short answer is the earth would be destroyed."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:05,440",
				"to": "00:00:08,400"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 5440,
				"to": 8400
			},
			"text": " There are limits to how fast you can push fluids through openings."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:08,400",
				"to": "00:00:13,120"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 8400,
				"to": 13120
			},
			"text": " For example, water always wants to boil, but is normally held together by air pressure."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:13,120",
				"to": "00:00:15,040"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 13120,
				"to": 15040
			},
			"text": " When a fluid flows through an opening fast enough,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:15,040",
				"to": "00:00:17,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 15040,
				"to": 17760
			},
			"text": " the pressure within the fluid drops due to the Bernoulli principle."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:17,760",
				"to": "00:00:19,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 17760,
				"to": 19680
			},
			"text": " Without enough pressure to keep the water from boiling,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:19,680",
				"to": "00:00:22,320"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 19680,
				"to": 22320
			},
			"text": " bubbles of steam form in a process called cavitation."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:22,320",
				"to": "00:00:24,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 22320,
				"to": 24880
			},
			"text": " Increasing the pressure to try to push the water through harder"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:24,880",
				"to": "00:00:27,040"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 24880,
				"to": 27040
			},
			"text": " surprisingly only makes it boil faster."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:27,040",
				"to": "00:00:29,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 27040,
				"to": 29760
			},
			"text": " Cavitation limits the total flow of water making it through the opening,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:29,760",
				"to": "00:00:32,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 29760,
				"to": 32880
			},
			"text": " though the higher the pressure, the faster the water steam mix will move"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:32,880",
				"to": "00:00:35,280"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 32880,
				"to": 35280
			},
			"text": " because more of it will expand into vapor bubbles."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:35,280",
				"to": "00:00:38,160"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 35280,
				"to": 38160
			},
			"text": " So how fast does Niagara Falls need to go to fit through a straw?"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:38,160",
				"to": "00:00:39,440"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 38160,
				"to": 39440
			},
			"text": " This is easy to figure out."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:39,440",
				"to": "00:00:43,440"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 39440,
				"to": 43440
			},
			"text": " All we need to know is the flow rate over the falls and how much area it needs to fit through."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:43,440",
				"to": "00:00:46,800"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 43440,
				"to": 46800
			},
			"text": " The flow rate over Niagara Falls is at least 100,000 cubic feet per second,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:46,800",
				"to": "00:00:48,480"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 46800,
				"to": 48480
			},
			"text": " which is actually mandated by law."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:48,480",
				"to": "00:00:50,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 48480,
				"to": 50880
			},
			"text": " A typical straw is about 7 millimeters in diameter."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:50,880",
				"to": "00:00:54,960"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 50880,
				"to": 54960
			},
			"text": " To find out how fast the water flows, we just divide the flow rate by that area."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:54,960",
				"to": "00:00:58,400"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 54960,
				"to": 58400
			},
			"text": " Apparently, our water will be going one quarter of the speed of light."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:58,400",
				"to": "00:01:00,800"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 58400,
				"to": 60800
			},
			"text": " On the plus side, we don't have to worry about cavitation anymore"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:00,800",
				"to": "00:01:02,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 60800,
				"to": 62720
			},
			"text": " because at those high energies everything's a plasma"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:02,720",
				"to": "00:01:05,280"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 62720,
				"to": 65280
			},
			"text": " and the concepts of boiling and cavitation don't even apply."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:05,280",
				"to": "00:01:09,120"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 65280,
				"to": 69120
			},
			"text": " Instead, the water molecules will be causing all kinds of exciting nuclear reactions."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:09,120",
				"to": "00:01:13,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 69120,
				"to": 73600
			},
			"text": " On the downside, no machine could actually accelerate that much water to relativistic speeds."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:13,600",
				"to": "00:01:14,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 73600,
				"to": 74880
			},
			"text": " But that's maybe for the best,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:14,880",
				"to": "00:01:17,440"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 74880,
				"to": 77440
			},
			"text": " since the power of the particle jet created by this scenario"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:17,440",
				"to": "00:01:20,240"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 77440,
				"to": 80240
			},
			"text": " would be greater than the power of all the sunlight that falls on Earth."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:20,240",
				"to": "00:01:23,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 80240,
				"to": 83680
			},
			"text": " Your waterfall would have a power output equivalent to that of a small star"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:23,680",
				"to": "00:01:26,000"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 83680,
				"to": 86000
			},
			"text": " and its heat and light would quickly raise the temperature of our planet,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:26,000",
				"to": "00:01:28,340"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 86000,
				"to": 88340
			},
			"text": " boil away the oceans and render the whole place uninhabitable."
		}
	]
}
